/-!
# Scheme-level vocabulary for Stacks Tags `0EYG` and `0EYH`

This file fixes the definitions in which the scheme-level forms of Abhyankar's lemma for a
regular divisor (Stacks Lemma 58.31.5, Tag `0EYG`, and Lemma 58.31.6, Tag `0EYH`) are stated,
and the affine statement that the scheme-level proof takes as a hypothesis.

## Definitions and their Stacks sources

* `IsEffectiveCartier D` — Stacks Definition 31.14.1 (Tag `01WR`) in the equivalent local form
  of Divisors, Lemma 31.14.2 (Tag `01WS`): near every point the ideal sheaf on an affine open is
  generated by one nonzerodivisor (equation `1` away from `D`).  This is the same local form as
  Tau Ceti's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsEffectiveCartier`; Mathlib at the pin has
  no effective Cartier divisors, and pcf does not depend on Tau Ceti, so it is defined here.
* `IsRegularScheme X` — Stacks Definition 28.9.1 (Tag `02IS`), verbatim: every point has an affine
  open neighbourhood whose ring of sections is Noetherian and regular (Mathlib's `IsRegularRing`
  includes Noetherianity).
* `IsTamelyRamifiedInCodimOne U f` — the definition in the text of Stacks Section 58.31 (Tag
  `0BSE`): for every prime divisor `Z ⊂ X` with `Z ∩ U = ∅`, with generic point `ξ`, the finite
  separable `K_ξ`-algebra `L_ξ = Γ(Y ×_X Spec K_ξ)` is tamely ramified with respect to `𝒪_{X,ξ}`
  (More on Algebra, Definition 15.113.7, Tag `09E9`, with `B`, `𝔪_i`, `e_i` as in Remark
  15.113.6).  A prime divisor disjoint from the open `U` is the closure of a point `ξ ∉ U` with
  `dim 𝒪_{X,ξ} = 1`.  The tame condition at a maximal ideal `𝔪` of the integral closure `B` of
  `𝒪_{X,ξ}` in `L_ξ` is pcf's `IsTamelyRamifiedAt` (ramification index invertible in `κ_A`,
  residue extension separable); this is Tag `09E9`'s condition, which in residue characteristic
  `0` is automatic for the separability and the index.  Decomposing `L_ξ` into fields and taking
  maximal ideals of each integral closure is the same as taking the maximal ideals of `B`.
  Section 58.31 imposes the standing assumptions "`U` dense" and "`𝒪_{X,ξ}` a discrete valuation
  ring" before the definition; they hold in the situation of `0EYG` and are not part of the
  predicate.
* `standardRing A f e = A[x]/(x^e - f)` and `standardTameRing A f e = C_f`, the two rings of
  Stacks Example 58.31.4 (Tag `0EYF`); `IsStandardTameData A f e` is that example's hypotheses
  (`A` Noetherian, `f` a nonzerodivisor, `A/fA` reduced, `e ≥ 1` invertible in `A`).

## The affine hypothesis

`Pcf.Stacks.AbhyankarLemmaTame R S a` (defined in `Pcf.Stacks.Abhyankar.Tame.Defs`, proved by
work package `A′` as `Pcf.Stacks.abhyankarLemma_tame`) is the affine statement used by the scheme
layer: `R` Noetherian, `a` a nonzerodivisor with
`R/(a)` regular, `S` finite over `R`, étale away from `a`, the integral closure of `R` in
`S[1/a]`, tamely ramified in codimension one along `V(a)` (pcf's
`IsTamelyRamifiedInCodimensionOneAlong`), imply at every `y ∈ V(a)` a pointed étale
neighbourhood `R → R'` with `R' ⊗_R S ≅ ∏ R'[x]/(x^{e_i} - u_i a)`, `e_i` invertible
(`HasAbhyankarStandardCoverAt`).  It is the characteristic-free analogue of phase 1's
`Pcf.Stacks.AbhyankarLemma` (whose hypothesis "every positive integer is invertible" is replaced
by tameness), and `abhyankarLemmaTame_of_natCast_isUnit` discharges it in the
characteristic-zero case from phase 1's `Pcf.Stacks.abhyankarLemma`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Limits TensorProduct

namespace Pcf.Stacks.SchemeLevel

/-! ### Effective Cartier divisors and regular schemes -/

/-- **Effective Cartier divisor** (Stacks Definition 31.14.1, Tag `01WR`, in the equivalent local
form of Lemma 31.14.2, Tag `01WS`): every point has an affine open neighbourhood `U` on which the
ideal of `D` is generated by a single nonzerodivisor of `Γ(X, U)`. -/
def IsEffectiveCartier {X : Scheme.{u}} (D : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ U.1 ∧
    ∃ a : Γ(X, U), a ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U) ∧ D.ideal U = Ideal.span {a}

/-- **Regular scheme** (Stacks Definition 28.9.1, Tag `02IS`): every point has an affine open
neighbourhood `U` such that `Γ(X, U)` is Noetherian and regular.  (Mathlib's `IsRegularRing`
contains Noetherianity.) -/
def IsRegularScheme (X : Scheme.{u}) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ U.1 ∧ IsRegularRing Γ(X, U)

/-- The open complement `X ∖ D` of the closed subscheme cut out by an ideal sheaf. -/
abbrev complementOpen {X : Scheme.{u}} (D : X.IdealSheafData) : X.Opens :=
  D.support.compl

/-! ### Tame ramification in codimension one (Stacks Section 58.31) -/

/-- The morphism `Spec K_ξ → X`, `K_ξ` the fraction field of the local ring `𝒪_{X,ξ}`. -/
noncomputable def specFractionFieldToScheme (X : Scheme.{u}) (ξ : X) :
    Spec (CommRingCat.of (FractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk ξ))) ⟶ X :=
  Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)
    (FractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)))) ≫ X.fromSpecStalk ξ

/-- The ring `L_ξ = Γ(Y ×_X Spec K_ξ)` of Stacks Section 58.31 for `f : Y → U ⊂ X`. -/
noncomputable def genericFibreRing {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens) (f : Y ⟶ U) (ξ : X) :
    CommRingCat.{u} :=
  Γ(pullback (f ≫ U.ι) (specFractionFieldToScheme X ξ), ⊤)

/-- `L_ξ` as a `K_ξ`-algebra, via the second projection `Y ×_X Spec K_ξ → Spec K_ξ`. -/
noncomputable instance genericFibreRing.algebraFractionRing {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens)
    (f : Y ⟶ U) (ξ : X) :
    Algebra (FractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)) (genericFibreRing U f ξ) :=
  ((pullback.snd (f ≫ U.ι) (specFractionFieldToScheme X ξ)).appTop.hom.comp
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (FractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)))).inv.hom).toAlgebra

/-- `L_ξ` as an `𝒪_{X,ξ}`-algebra, through `𝒪_{X,ξ} → K_ξ`. -/
noncomputable instance genericFibreRing.algebraStalk {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens)
    (f : Y ⟶ U) (ξ : X) :
    Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (genericFibreRing U f ξ) :=
  ((algebraMap (FractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)) (genericFibreRing U f ξ)).comp
    (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (FractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)))).toAlgebra

/-- **Tamely ramified with respect to `A`** (Stacks Definition 15.113.7, Tag `09E9`, with the
notation of Remark 15.113.6): every maximal ideal `𝔪` of the integral closure `B` of `A` in `L`
has ramification index invertible in `κ_A` and separable residue field extension. -/
def IsTamelyRamifiedOver (A L : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing L] [Algebra A L] : Prop :=
  ∀ m : Ideal (integralClosure A L), (hm : m.IsMaximal) →
    IsTamelyRamifiedAt A (integralClosure A L) ⟨m, hm.isPrime⟩

/-- **`Y` is tamely ramified over `X` in codimension one** (Stacks Section 58.31, Tag `0BSE`):
for every point `ξ ∉ U` with `dim 𝒪_{X,ξ} = 1` (the generic point of a prime divisor `Z` with
`Z ∩ U = ∅`), the algebra `L_ξ = Γ(Y ×_X Spec K_ξ)` is tamely ramified with respect to
`𝒪_{X,ξ}`. -/
def IsTamelyRamifiedInCodimOne {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens) (f : Y ⟶ U) : Prop :=
  ∀ ξ : X, ξ ∉ U → ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) = 1 →
    IsTamelyRamifiedOver (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (genericFibreRing U f ξ)

/-! ### Standard tamely ramified morphisms (Stacks Example 58.31.4, Tag `0EYF`) -/

/-- `A[x]/(x^e - f)`. -/
abbrev standardRing (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (f : A) (e : ℕ) : Type u :=
  AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ e - Polynomial.C f : Polynomial A)

/-- `C_f = (A[x]/(x^e - f))_f`, the source of the standard tamely ramified morphism
`Spec(C_f) → Spec(A_f) ⊂ Spec(A)`. -/
abbrev standardTameRing (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (f : A) (e : ℕ) : Type u :=
  Localization.Away (algebraMap A (standardRing A f e) f)

/-- The hypotheses of Stacks Example 58.31.4: `A` Noetherian, `f` a nonzerodivisor with `A/fA`
reduced, and `e ≥ 1` invertible in `A`. -/
def IsStandardTameData (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (f : A) (e : ℕ) : Prop :=
  IsNoetherianRing A ∧ f ∈ nonZeroDivisors A ∧ IsReduced (A ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) ∧ 1 ≤ e ∧
    IsUnit (e : A)

/-- The conclusion of Stacks Lemma 58.31.5 (Tag `0EYG`): étale locally on `X`, the morphism
`g : Y → X` is a finite disjoint union of standard tamely ramified morphisms
`Spec(C_f) → Spec(A_f) ⊂ Spec(A)`.  Precisely: every `x ∈ X` is in the image of an étale
`φ : Spec A → X` such that `Y ×_X Spec A → Spec A` is isomorphic over `Spec A` to
`∐_i Spec(C_{i, f_i}) → Spec A` with each `(A, f_i, e_i)` as in Example 58.31.4. -/
def IsEtaleLocallyStandardTame {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, ∃ (A : CommRingCat.{u}) (φ : Spec A ⟶ X), Etale φ ∧ x ∈ Set.range φ.base ∧
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → A) (e : Fin n → ℕ), (∀ i, IsStandardTameData A (f i) (e i)) ∧
      ∃ ψ : pullback g φ ≅ ∐ (fun i ↦ Spec (CommRingCat.of (standardTameRing A (f i) (e i)))),
        ψ.hom ≫ Sigma.desc (fun i ↦ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap A (standardTameRing A (f i) (e i))))) = pullback.snd g φ

/-- The local-structure clause of Stacks Lemma 58.31.6 (Tag `0EYH`): étale locally on `X`, the
morphism `π : Y' → X` is a finite disjoint union of morphisms `Spec(A[x]/(x^e - f)) → Spec(A)`
with `A` Noetherian, `f ∈ A` a nonzerodivisor with `A/fA` regular, and `e ≥ 1` invertible in
`A`. -/
def IsEtaleLocallyStandardRootCover {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (π : Y ⟶ X) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, ∃ (A : CommRingCat.{u}) (φ : Spec A ⟶ X), Etale φ ∧ x ∈ Set.range φ.base ∧
    IsNoetherianRing A ∧
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → A) (e : Fin n → ℕ),
      (∀ i, f i ∈ nonZeroDivisors A ∧ IsRegularRing (A ⧸ Ideal.span {f i}) ∧ 1 ≤ e i ∧
        IsUnit (e i : A)) ∧
      ∃ ψ : pullback π φ ≅ ∐ (fun i ↦ Spec (CommRingCat.of (standardRing A (f i) (e i)))),
        ψ.hom ≫ Sigma.desc (fun i ↦ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap A (standardRing A (f i) (e i))))) = pullback.snd π φ

/-! ### Affine charts -/

/-- Tameness of a chart `Spec B → Spec R_a ⊂ Spec R` in codimension one along `V(a)`, in the form
in which `IsTamelyRamifiedInCodimOne` reads on an affine open `Spec R` with `D = V(a)` and
`Y = Spec B`: at every prime `𝔭 ∋ a` with `dim R_𝔭 = 1` the algebra `K_𝔭 ⊗_R B` is tamely
ramified with respect to `R_𝔭`. -/
def ChartTame {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (a : R) (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] :
    Prop :=
  ∀ p : Ideal R, (_ : p.IsPrime) → a ∈ p → ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime p) = 1 →
    IsTamelyRamifiedOver (Localization.AtPrime p)
      (FractionRing (Localization.AtPrime p) ⊗[R] B)

/-- The affine form of the `0EYG` conclusion at a point `y`: a pointed étale neighbourhood
`R → A` of `y` with `A` Noetherian, `a` a nonzerodivisor of `A` with `A/(a)` regular, and
`A ⊗_R B ≅ ∏_i A_a[x]/(x^{e_i} - u_i a)` with `e_i ≥ 1` invertible in `A`. -/
def HasLocalizedStandardCoverAt {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (a : R) (B : Type u) [CommRing B]
    [Algebra R B] (y : PrimeSpectrum R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (A : Type u) (_ : CommRing A) (_ : Algebra R A), Algebra.Etale R A ∧
    (∃ y' : PrimeSpectrum A, y'.asIdeal.under R = y.asIdeal) ∧ IsNoetherianRing A ∧
    algebraMap R A a ∈ nonZeroDivisors A ∧ IsRegularRing (A ⧸ Ideal.span {algebraMap R A a}) ∧
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (e : Fin n → ℕ) (u : Fin n → Aˣ), (∀ i, 1 ≤ e i) ∧ (∀ i, IsUnit (e i : A)) ∧
      Nonempty (A ⊗[R] B ≃ₐ[A]
        ∀ i, AdjoinRoot (localizedStandardPoly (u i) (algebraMap R A a) (e i)))

/-- The affine form of Étale Morphisms, Lemma 41.18.3 (Tag `04HN`) at a point `y`: a pointed
étale neighbourhood `R → A` of `y`, `A` Noetherian, with `A ⊗_R B ≅ A^n`. -/
def HasSplitCoverAt {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B]
    (y : PrimeSpectrum R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (A : Type u) (_ : CommRing A) (_ : Algebra R A), Algebra.Etale R A ∧
    (∃ y' : PrimeSpectrum A, y'.asIdeal.under R = y.asIdeal) ∧ IsNoetherianRing A ∧
    ∃ n : ℕ, Nonempty (A ⊗[R] B ≃ₐ[A] (Fin n → A))

/-! ### The affine hypothesis (work package `A′`) -/

/-- **Characteristic-zero discharge of the affine hypothesis.**  If every positive integer is
invertible in `R`, then `AbhyankarLemmaTame R S a` holds, by phase 1's unconditional
`Pcf.Stacks.abhyankarLemma` (the tameness hypothesis is not needed). -/
theorem abhyankarLemmaTame_of_natCast_isUnit (R S : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (a : R) (hnat : ∀ n : ℕ, n ≠ 0 → IsUnit (n : R)) :
    AbhyankarLemmaTame R S a :=
  fun hR ha hreg hfin hetale hint _ y hy ↦
    Pcf.Stacks.abhyankarLemma R S a hR ha hreg hfin hetale hint hnat y hy

/-- The form in which the scheme-level theorems take the affine hypothesis: the affine
statement for every ring receiving a ring map from `Γ(X, ⊤)` (in the proof it is used only for
local rings `Γ(X, V)_𝔭` of affine opens `V`).  Work package `A′`'s theorem
`∀ R S a, AbhyankarLemmaTame R S a` discharges it outright. -/
def AbhyankarLemmaTameOver (X : Scheme.{u}) : Prop :=
  ∀ (R S : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (a : R),
    Nonempty (Γ(X, ⊤) →+* R) → AbhyankarLemmaTame R S a

/-- If every positive integer is invertible on `X` (a `ℚ`-scheme), the affine hypothesis holds
over `X` by phase 1. -/
theorem abhyankarLemmaTameOver_of_natCast_isUnit (X : Scheme.{u})
    (hnat : ∀ n : ℕ, n ≠ 0 → IsUnit (n : Γ(X, ⊤))) : AbhyankarLemmaTameOver X := by
  intro R S _ _ _ a ⟨φ⟩
  refine abhyankarLemmaTame_of_natCast_isUnit R S a fun n hn ↦ ?_
  simpa only [map_natCast] using (hnat n hn).map φ

/-- Work package `A′`'s universally quantified theorem discharges the hypothesis over every
scheme. -/
theorem abhyankarLemmaTameOver_of_forall (X : Scheme.{u})
    (h : ∀ (R S : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (a : R),
      AbhyankarLemmaTame R S a) : AbhyankarLemmaTameOver X :=
  fun R S _ _ _ a _ ↦ h R S a

end Pcf.Stacks.SchemeLevel
